# Ad and tracking hosts for the streaming apps, on top of dumbtv's Amazon list (ROADMAP section 2).
# Applied by debloat/ads.sh into personalDNSfilter's additionalHosts.txt. A host also blocks its
# subdomains. Found 2026-10-25 by opening each app's home screen (nothing played) and reading
# the filter's traffic log: Hotstar, FanCode, Airtel Xstream, SonyLIV and Prime Video. Prime's home
# made no ad calls (its ads are in the stream), and its Amazon telemetry is in dumbtv's list.
#
# In-stream video ads in Hotstar, Prime and FanCode come inside the video stream itself, so no
# host here removes them. These stop the trackers and the separately fetched ad calls.

# Trackers: analytics and crash reporting. Apps carry on without them.
app-measurement.com                  # Firebase Analytics (Hotstar)
appsflyersdk.com                     # AppsFlyer install attribution (FanCode)
mobile-collector.newrelic.com        # New Relic app monitoring (FanCode)
firebaselogging-pa.googleapis.com    # Firebase event logging (FanCode)
firebase-settings.crashlytics.com    # Crashlytics settings (FanCode, Hotstar, SonyLIV)
data.flurry.com                      # Flurry analytics (Airtel Xstream)
www.google-analytics.com             # Google Analytics (SonyLIV)
clevertap-prod.com                   # CleverTap engagement tracking (SonyLIV)
conviva.com                          # Conviva video analytics (seen in the log, app unknown)

# Ad calls: test each app after applying. If one breaks, move its line to the end with "!"
# (allow) in front, or run ads.sh --undo.
vmax-ads.fancode.com                 # FanCode's ad SDK (VMAX)
bifrost-api.hotstar.com              # Hotstar's ad platform: ad decisions and impression tracking
googleads.g.doubleclick.net          # Google ads (YouTube, IMA SDK in other apps)
static.doubleclick.net
adconfig.wynk.in                     # Airtel Xstream's ad configuration
events.airtel.tv                     # Airtel Xstream's own event tracking
evt.sonyliv.com                      # SonyLIV's own event tracking
